{"id": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/2026/09/04/the-wine-makers-disorganized-crime-the-smuggler-and-his-cellar/", "url": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/2026/09/04/the-wine-makers-disorganized-crime-the-smuggler-and-his-cellar/", "title": "🎧The Wine Makers – Disorganized Crime: The Smuggler and his Cellar", "summary": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"336\" src=\"https://wineindustryadvisor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/TWM_OG.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"radiomisfits.com\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"630\" src=\"https://wineindustryadvisor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/TWM_OG.jpg\" title=\"radiomisfits.com\" width=\"1200\" /></p>This week, we’re joined by “Rainbow Valentine” and her father, “Walter Lemur,” of the wildly popular podcast Disorganized Crime: Smuggler’s Daughter. Over the span of 10 episodes, Rainbow’s podcast tells the story of growing up in the drug-smuggling hippie counterculture of 1970s and ’80s Marin County. Walter was a particularly successful smuggler, and like many of his counterparts, he needed ways to launder all those ill-gotten gains. Some people bought vintage cars, art and antique jewelry, or made cash deals that skirted tax and banking laws. Walter did some of that, but early in his smuggling career he discovered a much more enjoyable way to invest his cash: fine wine. Shockingly, Sam grew up with Rainbow, only he knew her as Thesaly… Once he connected all the dots, we invited Thesaly and her dad to come on the show and tell some of his stories of wine “collecting.” We get into how “Walter” got into the business in the first place, some of the many dangers and complications along the way, and plenty of other meandering rambles. Most importantly, we dig into the wines he was investing in and what the world of fine wine was like in that heady era. “Rainbow” and “Walter” also brought a surprising treat: the last of six magnums Walter bought of 1952 Krug Champagne, supposedly from Rémi Krug’s personal cellar. The wine, like the stories, defied all logic and took us on a journey we could not possibly have predicted. Buckle up, open one up, roll one up and get ready for one of the wildest episodes of The Wine Makers Podcast yet! [Ep 427] Listen to Disorganized Crime and other great Rainbow Valentine podcasts here -&#62; https://rainbowvalentine.com/ (we highly recommend Psychadelic Women) Listen to the specific episode about wine buying and other cash cleaning tactics here -&#62; https://bit.ly/4crw8HU Follow Rainbow/Thesaly on Instagram- @rainbowvalentinelemur @theukulady", "content": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"336\" src=\"https://wineindustryadvisor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/TWM_OG.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"radiomisfits.com\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"630\" src=\"https://wineindustryadvisor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/TWM_OG.jpg\" title=\"radiomisfits.com\" width=\"1200\" /></p>This week, we’re joined by “Rainbow Valentine” and her father, “Walter Lemur,” of the wildly popular podcast Disorganized Crime: Smuggler’s Daughter. Over the span of 10 episodes, Rainbow’s podcast tells the story of growing up in the drug-smuggling hippie counterculture of 1970s and ’80s Marin County. Walter was a particularly successful smuggler, and like many of his counterparts, he needed ways to launder all those ill-gotten gains. Some people bought vintage cars, art and antique jewelry, or made cash deals that skirted tax and banking laws. Walter did some of that, but early in his smuggling career he discovered a much more enjoyable way to invest his cash: fine wine. Shockingly, Sam grew up with Rainbow, only he knew her as Thesaly… Once he connected all the dots, we invited Thesaly and her dad to come on the show and tell some of his stories of wine “collecting.” We get into how “Walter” got into the business in the first place, some of the many dangers and complications along the way, and plenty of other meandering rambles. Most importantly, we dig into the wines he was investing in and what the world of fine wine was like in that heady era. “Rainbow” and “Walter” also brought a surprising treat: the last of six magnums Walter bought of 1952 Krug Champagne, supposedly from Rémi Krug’s personal cellar. The wine, like the stories, defied all logic and took us on a journey we could not possibly have predicted. Buckle up, open one up, roll one up and get ready for one of the wildest episodes of The Wine Makers Podcast yet! [Ep 427] Listen to Disorganized Crime and other great Rainbow Valentine podcasts here -&#62; https://rainbowvalentine.com/ (we highly recommend Psychadelic Women) Listen to the specific episode about wine buying and other cash cleaning tactics here -&#62; https://bit.ly/4crw8HU Follow Rainbow/Thesaly on Instagram- @rainbowvalentinelemur @theukulady", "published_at": "2026-09-04 14:04:05+00:00", "source_name": "Wine Industry Advisor", "source_type": "media", "language": "en", "content_type": "market_report", "country": "US", "continent": "NEW_WORLD", "region": "Americas/North/USA", "producer_role": "trade_media", "trust_tier": "T3_professional", "info_purpose": ["P2_market_analysis"], "collection_tier": "C1_rss"}
